# Frozen captures are byte-exact: a test compares the committed bytes, so
# checkout must not rewrite them. Disable ALL text normalization for them.
#
# This is not hypothetical. `autocrlf=input` silently rewrote four captured
# pty logs so the committed blobs no longer matched their recorded SHA256SUMS
# (caught at commit ce8965e; a fresh clone would have failed the gate). The
# evidence tree those lived in is retired, but the rule outlived it: the list
# goldens under tests/fixtures moved out of that tree in slice Z4 and are
# `include_str!`d and compared byte for byte by `src/listing.rs`.
#
# Never remove without re-checking every byte-exact comparison from a CLONE.
tests/fixtures/** -text
